Rule 1 (ndarray's dtype in torch.from_numpy must be one of the supported dtypes)
{v_1 : dtype} |= v_1 = 0 ∨ v_1 = 1 ∨ v_1 = 2 ∨ v_1 = 3 ∨ v_1 = 4 ∨ v_1 = 5 ∨ v_1 = 6 ∨ v_1 = 7 ∨ v_1 = 8 ∨ v_1 = 9 ∨ v_1 = 10
>>
Rule 2 (tensor should have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 3 (The shape elements of the numpy array should not be negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (The ndarray should have a supported dtype for conversion to a tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 5 (The product of the dimensions of the array should be within the maximum value representable by int)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 0) < 2147483647
>>
Rule 6 (For complex type tensors, the corresponding numpy array also has to be a complex type.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 then true
